.\" ghost_story man page
.TH GHOST_STORY 1 "2026-11-04" "Ghost Story 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghost_story \- self-healing song builder for the Akai MPK Mini on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghost_story
<command> [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ghost_story
(Ghost Story) turns an Akai MPK Mini (mk1/mk2/mk3/Play, detected at runtime) plus a Linux
box with PipeWire into a complete song-building instrument: play keys and
pads, record loops with quantize and overdub, arrange patterns into a song,
mix with the hardware knobs, and export stems. No AI at runtime, no cloud,
no accounts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B play [\-\-headless] [\-\-seconds N] [\-\-project-dir DIR] [\-\-log-file PATH] [\-\-no-log-file]
Launch the app. Default is the native Qt6 window; \-\-headless runs the
engine without a display (CI / servers). \-\-seconds auto-stops.
Structured JSONL logs are appended to
.IR ~/.local/share/ghost_story/logs/app.jsonl ;
\-\-log-file overrides the path, \-\-no-log-file keeps stderr-only logging
(GHOST_STORY_LOG_FILE=0 does the same; any other value is a path).
.TP
.B doctor
Self-diagnosis: audio backend, MIDI ports, device manifest, disk space,
RT limits, journal integrity. Writes
.I doctor-report.json
and exits 0 only when every check passes.
.TP
.B repair
Verify/rebuild: re-probe the device manifest, replay and validate the WAL
journal, quarantine corrupt files. Writes
.IR repair-report.json .
.TP
.B bench [\-\-seconds N]
Audio-callback load test writing
.IR bench-report.json .
The M2 gate requires p99 callback < 30% of the buffer budget and zero
xruns; the default budget run is 300 s.
.TP
.B probe [\-\-capture]
Detect MIDI devices and write the checksummed device manifest to
.IR ~/.local/share/ghost_story/devices/device_manifest.json .
\-\-capture records 60 s of raw traffic (SysEx RE work).
.TP
.B export \-\-project-dir DIR (\-\-smf OUT.mid | \-\-wav-dir DIR)
Export the project: SMF type-1 MIDI, or offline-rendered per-track stems
plus master mix (32-bit float WAV; master equals the sum of stems).
.TP
.B version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ghost_story/devices/device_manifest.json
Detected device capabilities (checksummed, schema-versioned).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ghost_story/crashes/
Crash reports + safe-mode flag.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ghost_story/telemetry/sessions.jsonl
Local-only session telemetry. Set
.B GHOST_STORY_TELEMETRY=0
to disable all writes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ghost_story/logs/app.jsonl
Structured JSONL run log (rotates at 32 MiB, previous file kept as
.I app.jsonl.1 ).
Ship it to the development Kibana stack with
.IR make\ elk-up (deploy/elk/).
.TP
.I <project-dir>/project.journal
Write-ahead log; crash-safe with per-append fsync.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on failure; 2 on usage error; 3 when no device/clip is
found (probe/export).
.SH SEE ALSO
Docs in the repository: GARDENING.md (maintenance loop), ROADMAP.md,
docs/sysex.md (SysEx findings), docs/adr/ (architecture decisions).
